USB CDC ACM: cdc_acm_poll_out() flushes a full TX buffer instead of dropping.

6d69698de74 ("cdc_acm: tx throughput improvements", merged 2026-09-25)
replaced the TX ring buffer with net_bufs. poll_out() now only fills the one
`current` 64 B buffer, and moving on to the next is left to tx_fifo_work. A
printk burst from a thread that does not yield (a packet log line is 100-300 B)
fills that buffer and every further byte is discarded ("No TX buffer available,
discard data") because the work item cannot run meanwhile: RAW hex cut after
~64 B, RX lines losing their start, CLI replies such as `get public.key`
corrupted. The old ring buffer accepted ~1 KB per burst.

Enqueue the full buffer from poll_out() (thread context only) and retry once.
It never blocks, so an unplugged host cannot hang the caller; bytes are
dropped only when the buffer pool is exhausted, as before the rewrite.

Found 2026-09-26 with a rak3401_1watt repeater + packet_logging.conf feeding
mctomqtt. Not fixed on Zephyr main as of 3e7672a71bd; no upstream issue found.

diff --git a/subsys/usb/device_next/class/usbd_cdc_acm.c b/subsys/usb/device_next/class/usbd_cdc_acm.c
index 3957daa167b..5492f6c5ce4 100644
--- a/subsys/usb/device_next/class/usbd_cdc_acm.c
+++ b/subsys/usb/device_next/class/usbd_cdc_acm.c
@@ -1143,6 +1143,7 @@ static void cdc_acm_poll_out(const struct device *dev, const unsigned char c)
 	struct cdc_acm_uart_data *const data = dev->data;
 	k_spinlock_key_t key;
 	uint32_t wrote;
+	bool flushed = false;
 
 	while (true) {
 		key = k_spin_lock(&data->lock);
@@ -1153,6 +1154,18 @@ static void cdc_acm_poll_out(const struct device *dev, const unsigned char c)
 			break;
 		}
 
+		/* ZephCore: the current buffer is full. Hand it to the USB stack
+		 * now and continue in a fresh one from the pool, rather than
+		 * discarding until tx_fifo_work runs (it cannot run while this
+		 * thread is inside a long printk burst). Drops only once the pool
+		 * itself is exhausted, as the old ring buffer did.
+		 */
+		if (!flushed && !k_is_in_isr()) {
+			flushed = true;
+			cdc_acm_tx_fifo_enqueue(dev);
+			continue;
+		}
+
 		if (k_is_in_isr() || !data->flow_ctrl) {
 			LOG_WRN_ONCE("No TX buffer available, discard data");
 			goto cdc_acm_poll_out_schedule;
